3.difference between joins ?
A. Inner join - Returns only matching rows from both tables.
   left join - Returns all rows from the left table, and matching rows from the right table.
   right join - Returns all rows from the Right table, and matching rows from the left table.
   full join - Returns all rows from both tables, if no matched rown provides with null values.
   cross join -Returns a cartesian product – all combinations of rows from both tables.
