6. in python difference between copy and deep copy ?
A.Creates a new object and recursively copies all nested objects.
  Original and copied objects are fully independent.
  import copy

original = [[1, 2], [3, 4]]
deep = copy.deepcopy(original)

deep[0][0] = 100
print(original)  # [[1, 2], [3, 4]] → unchanged
  Creates a new object, but does NOT copy nested objects.
  The outer object is copied, but inner objects are shared (referenced).
  import copyc

original = [[1, 2], [3, 4]]
shallow = copy.copy(original)

shallow[0][0] = 100
print(original) 
  
